1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:15,000
残酷な天使のように 少年よ 神話になれ

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:37,000
青い風が今 胸のドアを叩いても 私だけをただ見つめて 微笑んでるあなた

3
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:51,000
そっとくれるもの 求めることに夢中で 運命さえまだ知らない 痛い気な瞳

4
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:58,000
だけどいつか気づくでしょう その背中には

5
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:07,000
遥か未来 目指すための羽があること

6
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
残酷な天使の転生 窓辺からやがて到達

7
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:22,000
もっと走る熱いパッドスで 思い出を裏切るなら

8
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:30,000
この空を抱いて輝く 少年よ 神話になれ

9
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
エリア!

10
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:05,920
ここにスペシ sol

11
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:10,000
や take out Curriculum

12
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
vastが終わりだ

13
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,080
お前たと一つタイカイの組メントに 厳しい

14
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:20,000
よいことに話 全体の公斤を迫させやして

15
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,320
Yes, I'm afraid so. Unit 4 is gone, alone with the second branch of nerve.

16
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:28,040
It happened while they were testing the S2 engine.

17
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:30,480
But don't worry, we'll be all right.

18
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:34,920
All three of our Avas are functioning properly, and our pilots and staff are in good shape, too.

19
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:37,620
I also heard that Unit 3 is being brought here.

20
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:40,680
You're performing the activation test at Matsushiro, aren't you?

21
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:44,760
Uh-huh. I'll be out for four days or so, but don't worry.

22
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:46,480
Akashi's coming over to take care of you guys.

23
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:47,680
But what about the test?

24
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:49,880
Oh, Ritsuko will be supervising everything.

25
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,360
There won't be any problems.

26
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:52,460
And who will be the pilot?

27
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:56,000
Well, the pilot is...

28
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:03,000
Yes?

29
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:09,140
Good morning, Major Katsuragi. I've come to ask for your help.

30
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:14,540
I'm begging you. Please, please, you've just got to choose me as the pilot for Evangelion Unit 3.

31
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:15,300
You gotta!

32
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:24,460
So, Shinji still doesn't know, huh?

33
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:31,760
I just can't find a chance to tell him. I'm worried. Sometimes I just can't figure out what he's thinking about.

34
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:35,640
Oh, get a grip, kid. You're the one who wanted to be his guardian.

35
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:38,060
Yeah, you're right, of course.

36
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:42,300
Um, so, when will you acquire the new pilot?

37
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:45,320
Tomorrow. There's still a few details to be ironed out.

38
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:48,200
Maybe the new pilot will tell Shinji himself.

39
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:58,960
Oh, no, I rather doubt it. This one wasn't very enthused about the prospect at all. He won't talk. He only accepted under the condition that his younger sister be transferred into our private hospital.

40
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:09,180
How can Miss Otto be so cruel? I'm dying to be pilot. So why won't she use me, even as a backup pilot? It's just not fair.

41
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:11,060
Mm-hmm. Yeah.

42
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:19,200
Hey, what's up? You left before me, but you're getting here late.

43
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:22,040
Oh, no fight between the newlyweds today?

44
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:29,720
Ah! I just didn't want to see your ugly faces, you damn three-studious-feduct idiot!

45
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:31,940
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

46
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:38,980
Ah, the precious moment of lunchtime. Hey, where's Toji?

47
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:40,440
I haven't seen him.

48
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:45,900
You mean he left? Without his lunch? Toji the stomach? That's impossible!

49
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:48,400
Hmm. Well, he's been acting different.

50
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,160
Mr. Sousaha?

51
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,540
Huh? Oh, it's you, Ayanami.

52
00:04:57,540 --> 00:05:00,020
Hey, if you're looking for Shinji, he's not here.

53
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:04,040
You know, don't you, about everything?

54
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:06,120
I think Asuka knows, too.

55
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:07,440
Hmm.

56
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:10,420
So, Shinji's the only one who doesn't know.

57
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:14,560
You know, it's pretty rare for you to be concerned about someone else.

58
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:17,420
It is? I'm not sure I understand.

59
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:19,960
Oh, you have a thing about Shinji, all right.

60
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:20,380
I?

61
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:23,480
Maybe that is true.

62
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:24,760
You do.

63
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:24,840
You do.

64
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:28,540
Hikari!

65
00:05:28,540 --> 00:05:29,540
Let's have lunch together!

66
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:30,540
Okay.

67
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:34,540
He's over two hours late, but last he's finally here.

68
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:36,540
This is the first time I've ever waited for someone this long.

69
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:38,540
That's because you never waited for guys back when you could still get a date.

70
00:05:38,540 --> 00:05:39,540
Oh, shut up.

71
00:05:39,540 --> 00:05:40,540
This was the so-called second impact.

72
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:42,540
At that time, I was living in a place called Nebukawa,

73
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:55,540
but the rising water levels caused by the melting of Antarctica have buried it beneath the sea.

74
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:00,540
I'm sorry, newcomer, but I had to clobber you.

75
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:05,540
I had to beat you to work off my own anger.

76
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:20,540
Oh, I'm sorry, Asuka. You usually walk home with Shinji, don't you?

77
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:25,540
I only walk with Shinji because we work together. And right now, I don't be like looking at him.

78
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:26,540
Oh.

79
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:31,540
This is about Toji, isn't it?

80
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:33,540
Yeah. How'd you know?

81
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:37,540
Everybody knows. The Three Stooges are the only ones who don't.

82
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:40,540
Shinji seems sensitive in a naive kind of way.

83
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:47,540
Shinji's a big fat dork. And he's denser than lead, too. He wouldn't know how to relate to another person if you gave him a manual.

84
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:49,540
Oh, I see.

85
00:06:51,540 --> 00:06:56,540
Asuka, I think that Toji might be interested in Rei.

86
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:59,540
Are you kidding? Toji and Wonder Girl?

87
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:01,540
Well, lunch, they seem...

88
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:08,540
Ha! Don't worry, Hikari. It'll never happen. If Shinji is denser than lead, then Rei Ayanami is off the atomic scale.

89
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:09,540
Really?

90
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:11,540
Yup.

91
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:15,540
Can I ask you something?

92
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:16,540
Uh, okay.

93
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:19,540
Just what do you see in a dumb jock like that?

94
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:23,540
It's the...contentioned sign.

95
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:24,540
What?

96
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:30,540
It was a mistake to get back with you.

97
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:32,540
How can you say that now?

98
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:36,540
There are a lot of pit holes in life, but you just have to dig your way out.

99
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:38,540
You know, Asuka...

100
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:40,540
Kashi sure spends a lot of time in the tub.

101
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:45,540
I wonder who's going to pilot Unit 3.

102
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:47,540
What? You mean you haven't heard?

103
00:07:47,540 --> 00:07:48,540
Who is it?

104
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:53,540
Yes. The only reason I came back to you was so we could break up again.

105
00:07:53,540 --> 00:07:54,540
I don't know.

106
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:56,540
Yeah, that was refreshing.

107
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:03,540
Are you two fighting again? I don't believe it. Are you two always like this whenever Katsuragi's gone?

108
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:13,540
It's not like that. I want to be happy, Kashi, especially since you're spending the night, but I can't. Not tonight. Not now. Not with everything.

109
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:20,540
I understand. Let's go to bed. I find that's usually the best thing to do in this kind of situation.

110
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:30,540
Hey, are you asleep yet, Kashi?

111
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:32,540
No, not yet.

112
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:35,540
Um, well, can you tell me what my father's like?

113
00:08:35,540 --> 00:08:39,540
Well, there's a surprise question. I would have thought you'd have asked about Katsuragi.

114
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:42,540
It seems like you're always with my father.

115
00:08:43,540 --> 00:08:48,540
Commander Fuyutsuki is the one who's always with him. Have you been asking around about your father?

116
00:08:48,540 --> 00:08:51,540
I just haven't been around him much.

117
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:54,540
So, you really don't know him.

118
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:57,540
But I've learned a lot about him lately.

119
00:08:58,540 --> 00:09:02,540
I've learned how he feels about his work. About my mother.

120
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:06,540
No, you're wrong, Shinji. You only believe that you've learned.

121
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:10,540
But people really can't understand themselves, much less each other.

122
00:09:11,540 --> 00:09:14,540
Understanding 100% of anything is impossible.

123
00:09:15,540 --> 00:09:19,540
That's why we spend so much time trying to understand our own motivations and those of others.

124
00:09:19,540 --> 00:09:22,540
That's what makes life so interesting.

125
00:09:22,540 --> 00:09:25,540
So, you can't understand Misato either.

126
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:29,540
The kanji that we use for the word she means a woman far away.

127
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:32,540
And women will always seem to be on a distant shore.

128
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:37,540
The gulf that separates male and female is broader and deeper than any ocean.

129
00:09:38,540 --> 00:09:40,540
I just don't understand adults.

130
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:45,540
T-minus 300 minutes to Unit 3 activation test.

131
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:47,540
Primary power standing by.

132
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:50,540
Repairs to left arm crimp lock completed.

133
00:09:50,540 --> 00:09:53,540
Refrigeration system in all sections function at standard levels.

134
00:09:54,540 --> 00:09:56,540
Roger. Team B, commence operation.

135
00:09:57,540 --> 00:09:59,540
Data link to Avangelion Unit 1 established.

136
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:02,540
The system's all up and ready for full activation.

137
00:10:03,540 --> 00:10:04,540
Terrific. Let's get started.

138
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:05,540
That was enthusiastic.

139
00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:10,540
You're aware that this unit will be assigned to your detachment once it's passed its tests, aren't you?

140
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:12,540
Exclusive control of four Avas.

141
00:10:13,540 --> 00:10:16,540
If you wanted to, you could conquer the world.

142
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:19,540
So, have you told Shinji yet?

143
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:21,540
I'll tell him after the test.

144
00:10:21,540 --> 00:10:27,540
The fourth child has arrived. Squad 2, begin entry preparations immediately.

145
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:31,540
Toji hasn't shown up yet, Asuka.

146
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:34,540
Yeah, he may not come today.

147
00:10:35,540 --> 00:10:38,540
I thought we might eat together today.

148
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:40,540
Do you want this?

149
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:45,540
Unit 3's already arrived in Japan, hasn't it?

150
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:47,540
Yeah, it got here yesterday.

151
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:51,540
This sucks. Who's gonna pilot it then?

152
00:10:52,540 --> 00:10:56,540
I told you was absent today. Maybe it's him.

153
00:10:57,540 --> 00:10:58,540
I don't think so.

154
00:10:59,540 --> 00:11:00,540
Entry plug secured.

155
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:01,540
Initiating burst connection.

156
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:04,540
Transmitting pulse. Graph readout is normal.

157
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:07,540
All checklists up to 1350 have been cleared.

158
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:10,540
Phase 1 contact all cleared.

159
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:12,540
Roger. Operation will proceed to Phase 2.

160
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:14,540
Full nerve link established.

161
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:16,540
Harmonics, level is 1055.

162
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:19,540
Harmonics are reading standard.

163
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:22,540
We are now approaching the absolute border.

164
00:11:24,540 --> 00:11:26,540
Break the nerve circuits! Abort the test!

165
00:11:27,540 --> 00:11:28,540
No! Mission failure!

166
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:31,540
We've got high energy readings in the body!

167
00:11:31,540 --> 00:11:32,540
An angel!

168
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:35,540
No!

169
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:56,540
There's been an explosion in Matsushiro!

170
00:11:57,540 --> 00:11:58,540
Damage level unknown.

171
00:11:59,540 --> 00:12:01,540
Send the rescue squad to 3rd Battalion.

172
00:12:01,540 --> 00:12:03,540
We've gotta handle this before the self-defense force gets involved.

173
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:05,540
Roger!

174
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:07,540
We've got an unidentified object detected at the site.

175
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:10,540
Its pattern is orange. We can't confirm that it's an angel yet.

176
00:12:10,540 --> 00:12:12,540
Go to first stage alert.

177
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:14,540
All personnel, go to first stage alert.

178
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:16,540
Prepare for surface to surface combat.

179
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:18,540
All AVAs, prepare for launch.

180
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:20,540
First for maximum intercept potential.

181
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:23,540
Air transportation to Matsushiro will go in 20.

182
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:31,540
An accident in Matsushiro? It can't be!

183
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:33,540
What happened to Misato?

184
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:35,540
Contact hasn't been restored yet.

185
00:12:36,540 --> 00:12:37,540
What are we gonna do? We need her.

186
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:39,540
We're gonna have to go for it ourselves.

187
00:12:40,540 --> 00:12:43,540
There aren't any other options left open for us, are there?

188
00:12:43,540 --> 00:12:45,540
But how can we find an angel without her?

189
00:12:46,540 --> 00:12:48,540
Commandry Curry will command this operation.

190
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:50,540
My father will?

191
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:53,540
We're receiving an image of the target from the Nobe Mountain Station.

192
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:55,540
Transferring to the main monitor.

193
00:12:55,540 --> 00:12:56,540
As we suspected.

194
00:12:56,540 --> 00:12:57,540
Transmit the abort signal.

195
00:12:57,540 --> 00:12:58,540
Eject the unit's entry plug.

196
00:12:58,540 --> 00:12:59,540
It's not working, sir.

197
00:12:59,540 --> 00:13:00,540
Neither the abort or plug ejection codes are being accepted.

198
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:01,540
What about the pilot?

199
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:04,540
His heart's still beating and he's still breathing.

200
00:13:04,540 --> 00:13:05,540
But he's probably...

201
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:06,540
I see.

202
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:08,540
Then we must accept the loss of Evangelion Unit 3.

203
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:09,540
Reclassify it as the 13th Angel.

204
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:10,540
What?

205
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:11,540
Sir.

206
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:12,540
Deploy our forces around the base of Mt. Nobe.

207
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:13,540
The target must be destroyed.

208
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:14,540
Target is approaching.

209
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:15,540
All units, prepare to engage.

